{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1786056561587,"sessionID":"ses_026bcee0cffeP4pQ8pfzLvxNoA","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"call_2e6ac31c40db47d3926592b9","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"People judge how random a sequence looks by tracking whether each toss\nrepeats the toss that came right before it, and they weight what happened\nmore recently more heavily. A sequence reads as random when its recent\ntosses keep flipping back and forth (few repeats, near 50-50), and reads\nas suspiciously structured when its recent tosses keep repeating the last\none — a long final run, or a run that grows back into a repeating tail,\nsignals a sticky process rather than a fair coin. Critically, this depends\non *where* the repetition falls: a burst of repetition at the very end\nweighs more than an equal burst early on, because the mental count of\nrun-continuations is recency-weighted. The model flags the louder repeat\ntail as non-random and the cleaner-recent sequence as random.\n","filePath":"/Users/ben/Documents/auto-psych/data/subjective_randomness/holdout_recovery_deepseek/holdout_runs/local_representativeness/experiment1/model_loop/iter_1/candidate_2/hypothesis.md"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/Users/ben/Documents/auto-psych/data/subjective_randomness/holdout_recovery_deepseek/holdout_runs/local_representativeness/experiment1/model_loop/iter_1/candidate_2/hypothesis.md","exists":false,"truncated":false},"title":"data/subjective_randomness/holdout_recovery_deepseek/holdout_runs/local_representativeness/experiment1/model_loop/iter_1/candidate_2/hypothesis.md","time":{"start":1786056561572,"end":1786056561585}},"id":"prt_fd9442f5e001jc4QpWSzVTPXGr","sessionID":"ses_026bcee0cffeP4pQ8pfzLvxNoA","messageID":"msg_fd943c5fc00190ORA9PsI8J630"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1786056565786,"sessionID":"ses_026bcee0cffeP4pQ8pfzLvxNoA","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"call_bc2673a1143a4a618a4379f9","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"recency_weighted_repetition\n","filePath":"/Users/ben/Documents/auto-psych/data/subjective_randomness/holdout_recovery_deepseek/holdout_runs/local_representativeness/experiment1/model_loop/iter_1/candidate_2/model_name.txt"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/Users/ben/Documents/auto-psych/data/subjective_randomness/holdout_recovery_deepseek/holdout_runs/local_representativeness/experiment1/model_loop/iter_1/candidate_2/model_name.txt","exists":false,"truncated":false},"title":"data/subjective_randomness/holdout_recovery_deepseek/holdout_runs/local_representativeness/experiment1/model_loop/iter_1/candidate_2/model_name.txt","time":{"start":1786056565780,"end":1786056565784}},"id":"prt_fd944559c001EdB4nYGmW3rTMb","sessionID":"ses_026bcee0cffeP4pQ8pfzLvxNoA","messageID":"msg_fd943c5fc00190ORA9PsI8J630"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1786056566080,"sessionID":"ses_026bcee0cffeP4pQ8pfzLvxNoA","part":{"id":"prt_fd9442ed4001XaECFqgUWILvhL","messageID":"msg_fd943c5fc00190ORA9PsI8J630","sessionID":"ses_026bcee0cffeP4pQ8pfzLvxNoA","type":"text","text":"A narrow stimulus set (runs + single alternations, max length 8) dominated by a near-perfect incumbent. All five existing hypotheses are global aggregate \"deviation-from-prototype\" accumulators. I'll propose a genuinely different mechanism — recency-weighted local repetition rate — which CONTEXT explicitly flags as invisible to all precomputed columns.\n\n","time":{"start":1786056552148,"end":1786056566075}}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1786056566206,"sessionID":"ses_026bcee0cffeP4pQ8pfzLvxNoA","part":{"id":"prt_fd94465bb001XItrEMTq5aYL0A","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"249b91d394e75cbbe990b19ff3899f695ad52294","messageID":"msg_fd943c5fc00190ORA9PsI8J630","sessionID":"ses_026bcee0cffeP4pQ8pfzLvxNoA","type":"step-finish","tokens":{"total":19336,"input":480,"output":2675,"reasoning":0,"cache":{"write":0,"read":16181}},"cost":0.001269268}}
