{"type":"text","timestamp":1786056580832,"sessionID":"ses_026bcee0cffeP4pQ8pfzLvxNoA","part":{"id":"prt_fd944970c001kVJhy9OOhPQF0m","messageID":"msg_fd944936c001lxLf4XRJnJvzWG","sessionID":"ses_026bcee0cffeP4pQ8pfzLvxNoA","type":"text","text":"All three files written and the self-check passes (`observed: chose_left`, featurizer columns registered, `p_left` finite via sigmoid).\n\n**Candidate: `recency_weighted_repetition`**\n\n- **Hypothesis** — people judge randomness by whether each toss repeats the previous toss, with *more recent* repetitions weighted more heavily; a recency-weighted repetition (run-continuation) rate drives the pairwise choice.\n- **Featurizer** — `compute_features` derives both a plain and an exponentially-decayed recency-weighted repetition rate per option (`rep_plain_a/b`, `rep_rec_a/b`), because no precomputed column sees position/recency.\n- **Model (2 free params)** — `alpha` (Beta, recency reliance) blends the plain and recency-weighted rates; `beta` (decision sensitivity) maps the contrast to `p_left` via sigmoid; Bernoulli likelihood on `chose_left`.\n\nThis is genuinely distinct from the incumbent and all four other hypotheses, which are global \"deviation-from-prototype\" accumulators; it diverges from them wherever a sequence has clean overall aggregate statistics but a repeating final tail.","time":{"start":1786056578828,"end":1786056580830}}}
